(2312250, 316307, 27482, '<td valign="top">I gotta say that I was a little bummed out not ribboning with a 7.15 but seeing this shot win was a great consolation.  First time seeing it too as I never vote on challenges I enter but even though I do that not to vote lower, I feel very confident that i still would have given this a 10 and of course added it to my favorites wich I just did.  <br/> <br/>Love everything about it and I think this is your best work as of this date.  AWESOME!  Could see this on the cover of National Geographic or Times or something like that.  Keep up the good work Manny, I know you are extremely good but you have proven time and time again that you can be better, two thumbs up :)</td>', 'I gotta say that I was a little bummed out not ribboning with a 7.15 but seeing this shot win was a great consolation.  First time seeing it too as I never vote on challenges I enter but even though I do that not to vote lower, I feel very confident that i still would have given this a 10 and of course added it to my favorites wich I just did.   Love everything about it and I think this is your best work as of this date.  AWESOME!  Could see this on the cover of National Geographic or Times or something like that.  Keep up the good work Manny, I know you are extremely good but you have proven time and time again that you can be better, two thumbs up :)', '2006-04-14 12:08:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2312260, 317751, 42100, '<td valign="top">The photos that really did well in this challenge really emphasized the texture with bright highlights and dark shadows.  This photo with the backlighting doesn''t emphasize the great texture of your subject.  I don''t think it''s a bad photo, I think it just didn''t move people to vote it at the next level.  The voting breakdown pretty much proves that by the lack of super low and super high votes.<br/> <br/>~Mark</td>', 'The photos that really did well in this challenge really emphasized the texture with bright highlights and dark shadows.  This photo with the backlighting doesn''t emphasize the great texture of your subject.  I don''t think it''s a bad photo, I think it just didn''t move people to vote it at the next level.  The voting breakdown pretty much proves that by the lack of super low and super high votes. ~Mark', '2006-04-14 12:14:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2312266, 315718, 18349, '<td valign="top">The score may be bad but I love the pic...Casa Rio is one of my FAVORITE places to eat and I adore the colorful umbrellas.  Best damned enchiladas in the state.  :)</td>', 'The score may be bad but I love the pic...Casa Rio is one of my FAVORITE places to eat and I adore the colorful umbrellas.  Best damned enchiladas in the state.  :)', '2006-04-14 12:17:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2312312, 317797, 22748, '<td valign="top">This is truly a stunning image. <br/> <br/>At a superficial (but critical) level, the focus and sharpness and lighting are great. Examining the composition, the way the her head angle creates leading lines draws the eye around the image, in addition to creating a great sharp region in the focal plane for the whole near side of her face. The color of the background is really elegant feeling next to the lizard''s body.<br/> <br/>Beautiful.</td>', 'This is truly a stunning image.  At a superficial (but critical) level, the focus and sharpness and lighting are great. Examining the composition, the way the her head angle creates leading lines draws the eye around the image, in addition to creating a great sharp region in the focal plane for the whole near side of her face. The color of the background is really elegant feeling next to the lizard''s body. Beautiful.', '2006-04-14 12:38:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2312316, 315575, 42792, '<td valign="top">Wow, thanks a lot guys!  My first 6 ... :D Really should thank hubby for pushing me to enter this one.  <br/> <br/>Appreciate all the helpful comments and constructive feedback.  Many pointed out the background would have been better blackened with no detail, even for my previous entry in Yellow.  Going by the high votes for such images, I certainly won''t disagree.  But I still stand with my choice not to do it that way.  I actually like the natural bits of subdued colour and design in the back as long as it doesn''t make the image look busy.  Guess it''s personal taste. :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Wow, thanks a lot guys!  My first 6 ... :D Really should thank hubby for pushing me to enter this one.   Appreciate all the helpful comments and constructive feedback.  Many pointed out the background would have been better blackened with no detail, even for my previous entry in Yellow.  Going by the high votes for such images, I certainly won''t disagree.  But I still stand with my choice not to do it that way.  I actually like the natural bits of subdued colour and design in the back as long as it doesn''t make the image look busy.  Guess it''s personal taste. :) ', '2006-04-14 12:40:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2312325, 316307, 42792, '<td valign="top">You''ve certainly raised the bar on this one!!!  Pekesty and I were having a private betting session during voting on this taking the blue!  Great great portrait - your best yet.</td>', 'You''ve certainly raised the bar on this one!!!  Pekesty and I were having a private betting session during voting on this taking the blue!  Great great portrait - your best yet.', '2006-04-14 12:47:05.000000', NULL, 0),
