(2322118, 314807, 38549, '<td valign="top">***Greetings from the Critique club***<br/> <br/>First off i have to say thank you for entering the challenge, its what keeps dpc going <br/> <br/>First off, i like your photo, <br/> <br/>Improves:<br/> <br/>Im unsure about your light, is that the light you wanted, or not (you should give a description of your photo in the comments box so we know what you tried to do)<br/>so to me i dont like the light, either a white or black ground, or even a bright colred one would work better, the backgroudn blends in to much with your subject,<br/> <br/>Sustains:<br/>Deph Of Field, is great, i really like it, <br/>you used the rule of thirds well<br/>its sharply in focus <br/>and your ideas are well used<br/> <br/>Good Job<br/> <br/></td>', '***Greetings from the Critique club*** First off i have to say thank you for entering the challenge, its what keeps dpc going  First off, i like your photo,  Improves: Im unsure about your light, is that the light you wanted, or not (you should give a description of your photo in the comments box so we know what you tried to do)so to me i dont like the light, either a white or black ground, or even a bright colred one would work better, the backgroudn blends in to much with your subject, Sustains:Deph Of Field, is great, i really like it, you used the rule of thirds wellits sharply in focus and your ideas are well used Good Job ', '2006-04-18 15:09:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2322972, 316509, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 5.  I know this plant <i>(or at least a few varieties of it)</i> and whilst you''ve captured it quite well, the freesias(?) dominated in this shot, in my opinion.  There were a few ''blown'' areas on the freesias as well.  Most importantly for this Challenge, the texture(s) were not captured to their full potential - again, my opinion.  Difficult with the ''composition'' and angle you have here, but perhaps just focussing in on the ''ice plant'' and the unusual textures of that, plus the boost with the colors, may have made this even better in my opinion. <i>edit:removed ''TN'', also, left a comment on your other shot of this plant.</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-19 06:45:12.</i></td>', 'I gave this a 5.  I know this plant (or at least a few varieties of it) and whilst you''ve captured it quite well, the freesias(?) dominated in this shot, in my opinion.  There were a few ''blown'' areas on the freesias as well.  Most importantly for this Challenge, the texture(s) were not captured to their full potential - again, my opinion.  Difficult with the ''composition'' and angle you have here, but perhaps just focussing in on the ''ice plant'' and the unusual textures of that, plus the boost with the colors, may have made this even better in my opinion. edit:removed ''TN'', also, left a comment on your other shot of this plant.', '2006-04-18 20:32:36.000000', '2006-04-19 07:45:12.000000', 0),
(2323914, 317086, 27164, '<td valign="top">Great shot, but the colors seems a bit awkward to me.  I bet it would have worked a lot better at sunrise/sunset.  Working from this shot, however, if it were me I''d probably have converted to B/W.</td>', 'Great shot, but the colors seems a bit awkward to me.  I bet it would have worked a lot better at sunrise/sunset.  Working from this shot, however, if it were me I''d probably have converted to B/W.', '2006-04-19 01:46:54.000000', NULL, 0),
